## Goal
Make the default `status` check always compare against the canonical install location (`~/Applications/Portero.app`) instead of whichever copy of the app is currently running. This came out of a cross-review.

## Problems
None.

## Decision
`installedApp()` in `cmd/portero/app.go` no longer returns the running bundle's path when one exists. It always returns `~/Applications/Portero.app`, the location `make install` maintains. If Launch Services launches a stale copy from somewhere else, the comparison now reports a mismatch instead of reporting "healthy" because the running copy matched itself. The old fallback for a bare CLI was already the standard path, so that case is unchanged.

The doc comment above the function still carries the old description, and a new one was added below it, so the comment is now duplicated and partly stale. A follow-up cleanup should remove the old line.

